<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seton Lloyd</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1902">1902</a>–<a href="/years/1996">1996</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Seton Howard Frederick Lloyd</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seton Lloyd was a British archaeologist who worked in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a> for much of the 20th century. As adviser to the Iraqi Directorate of Antiquities he excavated Tell Hassuna, Eridu and other sites with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fuad-safar">Fuad Safar</a>. He later directed the British Institute of Archaeology at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ankara">Ankara</a>, excavating Beycesultan, and wrote widely read books on the archaeology of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>.</p></div>
